---
title: The Lord's Prayer
type: prayer
citation: BCP 336
rite: I
---

[Celebrant] And now, as our Savior Christ hath taught us, we are bold to say,
[All] **Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy Name, thy kingdom come, thy will be done, on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread.**

---

[All] **And forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us. And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever and ever. Amen.**
